{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01241",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 5.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Morning, come on through. Did you come far?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.81,
      "end_seconds": 10.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Not too far, about half an hour by bus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.53,
      "end_seconds": 15.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.55,
      "end_seconds": 27.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "Yeah, um, it's sharp pain in the left chest when I breathe in. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.45,
      "end_seconds": 31.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.05,
      "end_seconds": 37.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Well, um, I've had it for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.53,
      "end_seconds": 50.62,
      "duration_seconds": 13.09,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. So, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.66,
      "end_seconds": 65.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.13,
      "text": "Um, I'd say once or twice a day. A seven out of ten, I suppose. Well, I had a sore throat earlier before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.29,
      "end_seconds": 72.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Have you had any palpitations, coughing up blood or recent long travel?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.66,
      "end_seconds": 77.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.63,
      "end_seconds": 84.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "So, and what about injury to the chest or breathlessness at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.77,
      "end_seconds": 92.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.8,
      "end_seconds": 95.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.11,
      "end_seconds": 99.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.16,
      "end_seconds": 108.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.45,
      "end_seconds": 115.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Yes, nickel. I get a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.93,
      "end_seconds": 134.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.77,
      "end_seconds": 139.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin. Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.12,
      "end_seconds": 147.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.43,
      "end_seconds": 152.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Alright, heart disease, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.76,
      "end_seconds": 165.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.62,
      "end_seconds": 170.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.92,
      "end_seconds": 175.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Right, are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.01,
      "end_seconds": 179.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.39,
      "end_seconds": 183.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.36,
      "end_seconds": 187.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.12,
      "end_seconds": 194.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.55,
      "end_seconds": 198.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.92,
      "end_seconds": 205.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.9,
      "end_seconds": 218.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.26,
      "text": "Iron tablets. I take it once a day. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. Ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, maybe, when it hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.41,
      "end_seconds": 224.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Right, do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.93,
      "end_seconds": 228.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.58,
      "end_seconds": 232.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.85,
      "end_seconds": 243.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.81,
      "end_seconds": 271.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 82, temperature is 36.7 degrees, saturation 98 percent, respiratory rate 16, blood pressure 115 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.63,
      "end_seconds": 278.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.0,
      "end_seconds": 284.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.59,
      "end_seconds": 289.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.53,
      "end_seconds": 293.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.5,
      "end_seconds": 297.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Right, take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.51,
      "end_seconds": 319.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "I can hear a faint rub on the left side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.09,
      "end_seconds": 322.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.28,
      "end_seconds": 339.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Air entry is equal on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.59,
      "end_seconds": 359.21,
      "duration_seconds": 15.62,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Okay, so my impression is this: I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at viral pleurisy or a clot in the lung that we should rule out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.0,
      "end_seconds": 362.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.34,
      "end_seconds": 370.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now viral pleurisy is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.6,
      "end_seconds": 382.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "We should do a chest X-ray for pleuritic pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.04,
      "end_seconds": 387.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.31,
      "end_seconds": 422.94,
      "duration_seconds": 34.63,
      "text": "I'll request an ECG, it'll help with chest pain. Regular pain relief makes it easier to take deep breaths, which protects the lung. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. One warning sign to remember: you become breathless or the pain changes. In that case don't wait. Please come and see me in a week. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.81,
      "end_seconds": 427.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.93,
      "end_seconds": 429.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}